al Observer Corps which enabled the RAF Fighter Command to establish a clear overview of the airspace over Britain. The Dowding System was not only used to control the fighter force, but also anti aircraft guns, searchlights and barrage balloons against the attacking Luftwaffe.","LocalizedString":"The Dowding System was an elaborate air defence network that was built by RAF before WWII and gave the British a critical advantage during the Battle of Britain. The system was the first ground controlled interception network that could cover such a large area. It used the British telephone network to collect information from radar stations and the Royal Observer Corps which enabled the RAF Fighter Command to establish a clear overview of the airspace over Britain. The Dowding System was not only used to control the fighter force, but also anti aircraft guns, searchlights and barrage balloons against the attacking Luftwaffe."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_depl_Fighter_small_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Fighters/AU_depl_Fighter_small_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Breakthrough/t_fighter_taking_off.t_fighter_taking_off","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Rebellion","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/dowding.dowding","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":681.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_dowding_system_photo","SourceString":"RAF operations room, between 1939-1945.","LocalizedString":"RAF operations room, between 1939-1945."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_Attac